#: input.md:1
msgid "Preparing the input files"
msgstr "入力ファイルの準備"

#: input.md:2
msgid ""
"The hySAS ONEBEAD mapping (1 bead for 1 amino acid, 3 beads for 1 "
"nucleodide) requires two PDBs, one for the MOLINFO and one for the TEMPLATE "
"actions. This applies to both SAXS and SAS modules. The MOLINFO PDB may "
"contain atoms, residues, chains, that are not included for the SAS signal "
"calculation, while the TEMPLATE PDB must contain only the residues that are "
"used for the ONEBEAD conversion. Some general rules:"
msgstr ""
"hySAS ONEBEAD（1アミノ酸に1 Bead、1 Nucleotide に3 Bead）には MOLINFO と TEMPLATE 用の2 "
"PDB が必要です。SAXS と SAS の両 Module に当てはまります。MOLINFO は対象外の原子・残基・Chain "
"を含められますが、TEMPLATE は変換対象の残基だけにします。一般規則は次です。"

#: input.md:4
msgid "1. Consistency between MOLINFO and TEMPLATE PDBs"
msgstr "1. MOLINFO と TEMPLATE の PDB の整合性"

#: input.md:5
msgid ""
"The numbering of atoms and residues must be consistent between the MOLINFO "
"and TEMPLATE PDBs. For example, if MOLINFO is provided with a PDB containing"
" 100 residues, but the SAS calculation is performed on residues in the range"
" 20-80, it is necessary to provide TEMPLATE with a PDB containing only these"
" residues, while maintaining their numbering: if the 20th residue starts "
"with atom number 319 and the 80th residue ends with atom number 1325, the "
"TEMPLATE PDB must start with ATOM 319 and residue number 20, and end with "
"ATOM 1325 and residue number 80. Warning: If a residue is included in the "
"SAS calculation, all corresponding atoms must be present in the PDB. Missing"
" atoms from a residue will cause the bead mapping step to fail."
msgstr ""
"Atom・Residue Number を一致させます。MOLINFO が100残基、SAS が20〜80だけなら、TEMPLATE "
"は番号を保持して20〜80だけにします。20が Atom 319から、80が1325までなら、ATOM 319・残基20から ATOM "
"1325・残基80までです。注意：対象残基の全原子が必要で、欠けると Bead Mapping が失敗します。"

#: input.md:7
msgid "2. Consistency between MOLINFO and the molfile"
msgstr "2. MOLINFO と Molfile の整合性"

#: input.md:8
msgid ""
"When using the plumed driver, the supplied molfile (PDB, XTC, ...) to be "
"analysed must be consistent with the PDB provided in MOLINFO. Specifically, "
"there must be the same number of atoms in the same order."
msgstr "driver の解析対象 Molfile (PDB、XTC など) は、MOLINFO と原子数・順序を一致させます。"

#: input.md:9
msgid "3. MOLINFO PDB numbering"
msgstr "3. MOLINFO PDB の番号"

#: input.md:10
msgid ""
"The MOLINFO PDB must start with ATOM number 1. The residue number can start "
"with a positive number other than 1."
msgstr "ATOM は1から始めます。Residue Number は1以外の正整数からでもかまいません。"

#: input.md:11
msgid "4. Providing the same file to MOLINFO and TEMPLATE"
msgstr "4. MOLINFO と TEMPLATE に同じファイルを渡す"

#: input.md:12
msgid ""
"It is possible to provide MOLINFO and TEMPLATE with the same PDB, taking "
"into account all three points above."
msgstr "上の3点を満たせば、同じ PDB を使えます。"

#: input.md:13
msgid "5. PDB format"
msgstr "5. PDB 形式"

#: input.md:14
msgid ""
"The naming conventions for atoms and residues can vary depending on the "
"force field or software used. This variability, particularly in the case of "
"nucleic acids, is a major limitation in the hySAS mapping process. Detecting"
" the residue type and analysing the atoms belonging to a bead is essential "
"to:"
msgstr ""
"原子・残基名は Force Field・ソフトウェアで異なり、特に核酸では hySAS Mapping の大きな制約です。残基種と各 Bead "
"の原子を特定する必要がある理由は、"

#: input.md:15
msgid ""
"calculate the Solvent-Accessible Surface Area, required to introduce the "
"solvation layer contribution or the hydrogen-deuterium exchange (SANS only);"
msgstr ""
"Solvation Layer や Hydrogen-Deuterium Exchange（SANS のみ）に必要な Solvent-"
"Accessible Surface Area を求めるため。"

#: input.md:16
msgid ""
"calculate the bead centre of mass, used to define the centre of the bead, a "
"feature which has a major influence on the final SAS profile calculation."
msgstr "最終 SAS Profile に大きく影響する Bead Center of Mass を求めるため。"

#: input.md:18
msgid ""
"For these reasons, as a preliminary step, each bead type and atom "
"composition is verified. In order to perform this process, it is not "
"feasible to consider all possible atom and residue names."
msgstr "そのため最初に Bead の型と構成原子を検証します。すべての命名を扱うことは現実的ではありません。"

#: input.md:20
msgid "Amino acids"
msgstr "アミノ酸"

#: input.md:22
msgid ""
"Several histidine residue names in different protonation states are "
"accepted: HIS, HIE/HID/HIP (AMBER), HSE/HSD/HSP (CHARMM)."
msgstr ""
"Histidine の Protonation に応じた HIS、HIE/HID/HIP (AMBER)、HSE/HSD/HSP (CHARMM) "
"に対応します。"

#: input.md:24
msgid ""
"Besides CYS, the cysteine involved in disulfide bridge is also allowed. In "
"the latter case, the residue name must be CYX."
msgstr "CYS に加え、Disulfide Bridge の Cysteine にも対応し、後者は CYX とします。"

#: input.md:26
msgid "Nucleic acids"
msgstr "核酸"

#: input.md:27
msgid ""
"Only the AMBER OL3 nomenclature for RNA residue and atom names, and the "
"AMBER OL15 nomenclature for DNA residue and atom names, are accepted. The "
"easiest way to convert a PDB to these formats is to use the pdb4amber script"
" which is part of the free [AmberTools](https://ambermd.org/AmberTools.php) "
"suite. This is the command:"
msgstr ""
"RNA は AMBER OL3、DNA は AMBER OL15 の命名のみ対応します。無料の "
"[AmberTools](https://ambermd.org/AmberTools.php) の pdb4amber で簡単に変換できます。"

#: input.md:32
msgid ""
"Warning: The `-d` `--add-missing-atoms` flags combination adds the hydrogen "
"atoms to the PDB even if they already exist with a different nomenclature. "
"This means that this step could double the number of atoms in the PDB. A "
"solution could be to remove the original hydrogens from the PDB allowing the"
" script to add them again with the correct nomenclature. Note that the order"
" of the atoms in the MOLINFO and TEMPLATE PDBs, as well as in a previously "
"generated trajectory to be analysed with the driver, must be consistent."
msgstr ""
"注意：`-d` と `--add-missing-atoms` "
"は、異なる名前の水素が既にあっても追加するため、原子数が倍になる場合があります。元の水素を除き、正しい命名で追加させる方法があります。MOLINFO、TEMPLATE、既存"
" Trajectory の原子順序を一致させてください。"

#: input.md:34
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the LEaP script, also part of the AmberTools suite, can "
"convert the PDB. Here is a quick step-by-step guide:"
msgstr "AmberTools の LEaP でも変換できます。手順を示します。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: input.md:35
msgid "RNA"
msgstr "RNA"

#: input.md:36
msgid "create a `leapRNA.in` file:"
msgstr "`leapRNA.in` を作る。"

#: input.md:40 input.md:65
msgid "copy the following instructions and save the file:"
msgstr "次を Copy して保存する。"

#: input.md:50
msgid "Command details:"
msgstr "コマンドの詳細："

#: input.md:52
msgid ""
"`source leaprc.RNA.OL3`: Load the parameter set for RNA molecules, "
"specifically the OL3 force field parameters. `rna_molecule = loadpdb "
"original_RNA.pdb`: Load the RNA molecule from the specified PDB file "
"(original_RNA.pdb) into the LEaP program and assign it to the variable "
"rna_molecule. Replace original_RNA.pdb with the PDB name you wish to "
"convert. `savepdb rna_molecule RNA_amber.pdb`: Save the RNA molecule that "
"was loaded into the LEaP environment into a new PDB file named "
"RNA_amber.pdb. This new PDB file will be formatted according to the "
"conventions used by the AMBER software suite. Replace \"RNA_amber.pdb` with "
"your preferred PDB name."
msgstr ""
"`source leaprc.RNA.OL3`：RNA の OL3 パラメータを読む。`rna_molecule = loadpdb "
"original_RNA.pdb`：original_RNA.pdb を読み、rna_molecule に代入する。original_RNA.pdb "
"は対象名に置き換える。`savepdb rna_molecule RNA_amber.pdb`：AMBER 形式の RNA_amber.pdb "
"に保存する。RNA_amber.pdb は希望の出力名に変える。"

#: input.md:56 input.md:75
msgid "Run LEaP:"
msgstr "LEaP を実行する。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: input.md:60
msgid "DNA"
msgstr "DNA"

#: input.md:61
msgid "create a `leapDNA.in` file:"
msgstr "`leapDNA.in` を作る。"

#: input.md:79
msgid "6. Special beads"
msgstr "6. 特殊な Bead"

#: input.md:80
msgid "DNA and RNA"
msgstr "DNA と RNA"

#: input.md:81
msgid ""
"Three additional bead types are available for DNA and RNA besides phosphate "
"group, pentose sugar, and nucleobase:"
msgstr "Phosphate、Pentose Sugar、Nucleobase に加え、3つの型があります。"

#: input.md:82
msgid ""
"5'-end pentose sugar capped with a hydroxyl moiety at C5'. To enable this, "
"the residue name in the PDB must be followed by \"5\". For example, in the "
"case of cytosine, the corresponding residue must be edited to DC5 or to C5 "
"in DNA and RNA, respectively."
msgstr ""
"C5' に Hydroxyl を持つ5'末端 Pentose Sugar。残基名に「5」を加えます。Cytosine なら DNA は DC5、RNA "
"は C5 です。"

#: input.md:83
msgid ""
"3'-end pentose sugar capped with an hydroxyl moiety at C3'. To enable this, "
"the residue name in the PDB must be followed by \"3\". For example, in the "
"case of cytosine, the corresponding residue must be edited to DC3 or to C3 "
"in DNA and RNA, respectively."
msgstr ""
"C3' に Hydroxyl を持つ3'末端 Pentose Sugar。残基名に「3」を加えます。Cytosine なら DNA は DC3、RNA "
"は C3 です。"

#: input.md:84
msgid ""
"5'-phosphorylated end with an additional hydroxyl moiety at P. To enable "
"this, the residue name in the PDB must be followed by \"T\". For example, in"
" the case of cytosine, the corresponding residue must be edited to DCT or to"
" CT in DNA and RNA, respectively. The additional O atom can be named in the "
"PDB as OP3 or O3P, while the additional H can be named HOP3."
msgstr ""
"P に Hydroxyl を持つ5'-Phosphorylated 末端。残基名に「T」を加えます。Cytosine なら DNA は DCT、RNA "
"は CT です。追加酸素は OP3 または O3P、水素は HOP3 とします。"

#: input.md:87
msgid "Proteins"
msgstr "タンパク質"

#: input.md:88
msgid "An additional bead type is available for proteins:"
msgstr "追加の型は、"

#: input.md:89
msgid ""
"Cysteine residue involved in disulfide bridge (the residue in the PDB must "
"be named CYX)."
msgstr "Disulfide Bridge の Cysteine（PDB 残基名 CYX）。"

#: input.md:91
msgid "7. Atom names"
msgstr "7. 原子名"

#: input.md:92
msgid ""
"For practical purposes, the table below lists all DNA/RNA atom names "
"accepted for each bead category. Note that an additional bead check is "
"performed to ensure that the correct atom is associated with the correct "
"nucleotidee bead type. For example, if an O2' atom name is detected in a "
"thymine bead, an error message is triggered."
msgstr ""
"次表は各 DNA/RNA Bead が受け付ける原子名です。正しい原子が正しい Nucleotide Bead に対応するか追加確認します。例えば "
"Thymine に O2' があるとエラーです。"

#: input.md:94
msgid "Pentose Bead Atoms"
msgstr "Pentose Bead の原子"

#: input.md:94
msgid "Nucleobase Bead Atoms"
msgstr "Nucleobase Bead の原子"

#: input.md:94
msgid "PO Bead Atoms"
msgstr "PO Bead の原子"

